UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Four of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Stabilization"—the triumphant moment where the kinetic energy of the Ace through the Three manifests as a stable, high-resonance structure, a foundation upon which a more complex, communal reality can be built. Moving beyond the speculative expansion of the Three, the Four signifies the phase of "integration and celebration," where the sovereign consciousness has successfully secured a territory and is now reaping the benefits of its strategic alignment. Visually represented by four staves topped with a blossoming canopy of flowers, this archetype embodies the concept of "homeostatic excellence"—a state where your environment has been brought into such perfect, harmonious alignment with your internal intent that it serves as a secure, high-utility base of operations. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "structural validation," where the feedback loops between your inner drive and your external results are no longer just functional, but are actively generating an ambient field of joy, belonging, and sustainable creative potential. When the Four of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Hardened Infrastructure" status; the work of the previous phases has crystallized into a reality that you can now inhabit, enjoy, and leverage for even greater, future-oriented maneuvers. This is the archetype of the "Consecrated Space," the place where you can safely lower your defenses because the integrity of your surroundings is guaranteed by your own, prior discipline. It commands you to recognize the significance of this milestone, to honor the labor that built it, and to participate in the collective resonance it creates. You are being tasked with the essential work of "celebratory maintenance": maintaining the high-frequency integrity of this space while allowing yourself the necessary, ego-stripping work of being fully present within it, rather than immediately rushing toward the next objective. To inhabit the Four of Wands is to master the art of "grounded manifestation," understanding that true mastery is not just the ability to create, but the ability to build a structure that can sustain that creation over time, providing a reliable home for your evolving, high-vibration soul-intent.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Four of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "structural degradation," "domestic dissonance," or the systemic collapse of the foundational container you have worked so hard to establish. The reversal suggests that the stability you are experiencing is brittle, performative, or increasingly incompatible with the current, higher-frequency requirements of your soul-evolution. You are essentially "living in a house of cards," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script to project an image of "attainment" or "celebration" while the structural pillars are silently rotting beneath the surface. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: your outer world may be designed to resemble a Four of Wands—orderly, successful, connected—but the frequency is failing, leading to a profound, chronic sense of displacement, alienation, and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current environment is no longer a "home" but a cage of your own, outdated design. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of preservation"; you are obsessively clinging to the external markers of success—the house, the tribe, the status—even as the internal resonance that originally validated those structures has evaporated. The reversed Four of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of admitting that your "base of operations" is no longer functional, and the fear that if you were to dismantle it, you would lose the last, fragile vestige of your own perceived stability. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these maintain-the-facade scripts, perform a brutal audit of your current structural foundations, and confront the reality of why you are prioritizing the "image" of security over the "substance" of authentic, evolutionary alignment. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a failing reality, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual integrity. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of structural renewal—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having outgrown the container you created, and realizing that until you are willing to let the false stability crumble, you will continue to be starved by the very structures you worked so hard to manifest.'
WHERE id = 18;
